From 98148c94ea753fab2b236ce9e6f2b1522926afd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arena-agent <arena-agent@local>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 11:19:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Show elapsed time while the signer is being set up
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A second report from the field came back at stage: setup with no percentage,
and the screen had said "setting up the signer, this takes about a minute" —
one static line, for the longest wait in the whole flow. That is
indistinguishable from a dead tab.

It is not a stall. The worker posts phase:setup before Signer.create() and then
enters one blocking call — Machine.open, initialize, two exchange rounds — from
inside which it cannot report at all. The client's own timeout is 15 minutes, so
for up to 15 minutes the line neither changes nor errors.

There is no honest percentage to invent for it, so it counts up instead: the
seconds move every second, which is the only available evidence that the worker
is still alive. The wording stops promising a minute, since the only
measurements that exist are WebKit 35 s, Node 63 s and desktop Chrome 115 s —
and the reports come from real phones, where none of those apply.

Also fixes the toast mock in DiagnosticsModal.test.tsx, which replaced the store
with a function returning the state instead of calling the selector, so addToast
was not a function and every run left an unhandled rejection behind the tests.

Verified by removing the timer and watching both new tests fail.
